Translation patch: parameter names in `row::convert` and `Row::place`

Change: In src/row/convert/mod.rs (outside the nightly-only bench), every parameter and local named `row` becomes `r` and every local named `value` (in the `take_or_place!` macro) becomes `v`; the same for the `row` parameter of `FromRow for HNil` (frunk.rs) and the `value` parameter of `Row::place` (row/mod.rs). Paths (`crate::row::..`, `value::..`), the macro's `$row` metavariable, comments and string literals are unchanged.
Why: Aeneas bug (as in patch 59): the generated Lean names definitions by module path (`row.Row.take`, `value.Value`), and a local variable `row` (or `value`) shadows that prefix, so Lean reads `row.Row..` as a field projection on the local ("Invalid field `Row`").
Behaviour: Identical: renaming.

